-- title:
--   From HTo GAdjacent Stage A0 Pointwise Left Shape
-- statement:
--   **Pointwise A0 rewrite to the left-action shape.** Fix a field-model parameter set, a bipartite state `psiBi`, an indexed polynomial family, natural numbers `ell` and `n`, a slice height $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, and a point tuple `xs` of length `n`. For each Boolean bit $b$, type pattern $\tau$, completed outcome $g$, and completed tuple outcome `gs`, use the recurrence weight $S$, indexed outcome operator $U$, and half-product operator $T$ defined from these data. The sum filtered by `g.isSome = b` and `gHatTupleType gs = tau` equals the unfiltered sum after the first move-right identity:
--   Write $\Theta$ for the parameter tuple, $F$ for the family, $b(g)$ for the genuine-outcome indicator, and $\tau(gs)$ for the tuple type.
--   $$
--   \sum_{b,\tau}\sum_{g:\,b(g)=b}\sum_{gs:\,\tau(gs)=\tau}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{\mathrm{bi}}}\left(L(UTT^{\mathsf H}U)R(S)\right)
--   =\sum_g\sum_{gs}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{\mathrm{bi}}}\left(\left(L(UTT^{\mathsf H})R(S)\right)L(U)\right).
--   $$
--
--   The filtered sums partition the completed outcome and tuple spaces by their Boolean type data. The result is used by `fromHToGAdjacentStageA0_eq_leftShape` before the slice and point averages are globalized.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGAdjacentStageA0_pointwise_leftShape`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
